WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.597 --> 00:07.070 align:center line:79%
My loving brothers and sisters,
thank you for your prayers in my behalf.

00:07.304 --> 00:08.839 align:center line:81%
I have felt them.

00:11.508 --> 00:16.547 align:center line:79%
The doctrine of The Church of Jesus Christ
of Latter-day Saints centers

00:16.547 --> 00:17.748 align:center line:81%
on the family.

00:18.882 --> 00:23.654 align:center line:79%
Essential to our doctrine
on the family is the temple.

00:24.955 --> 00:31.428 align:center line:79%
The ordinances received there enable us
to return as eternal families

00:31.962 --> 00:34.798 align:center line:81%
to the presence of our Heavenly Father.

00:36.800 --> 00:41.305 align:center line:81%
As of the April 2025 general conference,

00:42.172 --> 00:50.514 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson had announced
the construction of 200 new temples.

00:51.682 --> 00:57.421 align:center line:79%
He loved to announce new temples at the
conclusion of each general conference,

00:58.322 --> 01:00.490 align:center line:81%
and we all rejoiced with him.

01:02.593 --> 01:08.031 align:center line:79%
However, with the large number
of temples now in the very earliest phases

01:08.031 --> 01:10.200 align:center line:81%
of planning and construction,

01:11.201 --> 01:16.773 align:center line:79%
it is appropriate that we slow
down the announcement of new temples.

01:18.275 --> 01:22.913 align:center line:79%
Therefore, with the approval
of the Quorum of the Twelve Apostles,

01:23.614 --> 01:29.252 align:center line:79%
we will not announce any new temples
at this conference.

01:30.954 --> 01:36.093 align:center line:79%
We will now move forward in providing
the ordinances of the temple to members

01:36.093 --> 01:38.295 align:center line:81%
of the Church throughout the world,

01:39.162 --> 01:47.004 align:center line:79%
including when and where to announce
the construction of new temples.

01:53.543 --> 01:55.145 align:center line:81%
The portion of my talk

01:57.180 --> 02:00.917 align:center line:79%
that I have just delivered
was written after the death

02:00.917 --> 02:04.221 align:center line:79%
of our beloved president,
Russell M. Nelson.

02:05.822 --> 02:10.627 align:center line:79%
What follows now was written
and approved weeks before,

02:11.895 --> 02:17.300 align:center line:79%
but it still represents my teachings
inspired by the Lord.

02:20.137 --> 02:24.975 align:center line:79%
The family proclamation
announced exactly 30 years ago,

02:25.876 --> 02:29.212 align:center line:79%
declares that “the family
is ordained of God”

02:29.880 --> 02:35.952 align:center line:79%
and “is central to the Creator’s plan
for the eternal destiny of His children.”

02:37.120 --> 02:42.826 align:center line:79%
It also declares “that God’s commandment
for His children to multiply

02:42.826 --> 02:46.496 align:center line:81%
and replenish the earth remains in force.”

02:47.497 --> 02:54.271 align:center line:79%
And “we further declare that God
has commanded that the sacred powers

02:54.271 --> 02:59.476 align:center line:79%
of procreation are to be employed
only between man and woman,

02:59.476 --> 03:03.146 align:center line:81%
lawfully wedded as husband and wife.”

03:05.982 --> 03:11.054 align:center line:79%
As then Elder Russell M. Nelson
taught a BYU audience,

03:12.122 --> 03:16.460 align:center line:79%
the family is, quote,
“pivotal to God’s plan. ...

03:17.227 --> 03:23.300 align:center line:79%
In fact, a purpose
of the plan is to exalt the family.”

03:23.300 --> 03:24.301 align:center line:81%
End of quote.

03:26.570 --> 03:32.776 align:center line:79%
The Church of Jesus Christ is sometimes
known as a family-centered church.

03:33.210 --> 03:36.780 align:center line:81%
It is! Our relationship to God

03:36.780 --> 03:42.219 align:center line:79%
and the purpose of our mortal
life are explained in terms of the family.

03:43.353 --> 03:49.893 align:center line:79%
The gospel of Jesus Christ is the plan
of our Heavenly Father for the benefit

03:49.893 --> 03:51.695 align:center line:81%
of His spirit children.

03:52.829 --> 03:59.402 align:center line:79%
We can truly say that the gospel
plan was first taught to us in the council

03:59.402 --> 04:01.271 align:center line:81%
of an eternal family.

04:02.139 --> 04:06.176 align:center line:79%
It is implemented
through our mortal families,

04:06.910 --> 04:14.951 align:center line:79%
and its intended destiny is to exalt
the children of God in eternal families.

04:16.586 --> 04:19.022 align:center line:81%
Despite that doctrinal context,

04:19.055 --> 04:21.191 align:center line:81%
there is opposition.

04:22.325 --> 04:23.860 align:center line:81%
In the United States,

04:23.860 --> 04:29.966 align:center line:79%
we are suffering from a deterioration
in marriage and childbearing.

04:31.201 --> 04:32.936 align:center line:81%
For nearly 100 years,

04:32.936 --> 04:38.809 align:center line:79%
the proportion of households
headed by married couples has declined,

04:39.509 --> 04:41.511 align:center line:81%
and so has the birthrate.

04:42.913 --> 04:48.652 align:center line:79%
The marriages and birth rates of our
Church members are much more positive,

04:48.885 --> 04:53.657 align:center line:81%
but they have also declined significantly.

04:55.525 --> 05:00.263 align:center line:79%
It is vital that Latter-day
Saints do not lose their understanding

05:00.263 --> 05:04.668 align:center line:79%
of the purpose of marriage
and the value of children.

05:05.602 --> 05:08.872 align:center line:81%
That is the future for which we strive.

05:10.473 --> 05:17.848 align:center line:79%
“Exaltation is a family affair,
President Nelson has taught us.

05:17.848 --> 05:22.152 align:center line:79%
Quote, “Only through the saving
ordinances of the gospel

05:22.152 --> 05:26.523 align:center line:81%
of Jesus Christ can families be exalted.”

05:27.324 --> 05:28.358 align:center line:81%
End of quote.

05:30.527 --> 05:32.929 align:center line:81%
The national declines in marriage

05:32.929 --> 05:37.701 align:center line:79%
and childbearing are understandable
for historic reasons,

05:38.535 --> 05:42.272 align:center line:79%
but Latter-day Saint values
and practices should improve—

05:42.639 --> 05:44.808 align:center line:81%
not follow—those trends.

05:46.776 --> 05:49.679 align:center line:81%
In my boyhood, 70 years ago,

05:50.580 --> 05:54.517 align:center line:81%
I lived on my grandparents’ farm

05:55.118 --> 05:58.054 align:center line:79%
in a setting where
almost all that happened

05:58.054 --> 06:02.525 align:center line:79%
during the day was under
the direction of the family.

06:03.493 --> 06:04.995 align:center line:81%
There was no television

06:04.995 --> 06:09.499 align:center line:79%
or other electronics to distract
from family activities.

06:10.734 --> 06:14.804 align:center line:79%
In contrast, in today’s
urban society,

06:14.804 --> 06:22.312 align:center line:79%
few members experience consistent,
family-centered activities. Urban living

06:22.312 --> 06:24.214 align:center line:81%
and modern transportation,

06:24.714 --> 06:26.449 align:center line:81%
organized entertainment,

06:26.449 --> 06:32.789 align:center line:79%
and high-speed communication have made
it easy for youth to treat their homes

06:32.789 --> 06:37.227 align:center line:79%
as boarding houses where they sleep
and take an occasional meal,

06:37.861 --> 06:43.199 align:center line:79%
but where there is far less
parental direction of their activities.

06:45.368 --> 06:49.272 align:center line:79%
Parental influences
have also been diluted by the way in

06:49.272 --> 06:53.476 align:center line:79%
which most current members
of the Church earn a living.

06:54.611 --> 06:59.749 align:center line:79%
In times past, one of the great
influences that unified

06:59.749 --> 07:05.789 align:center line:79%
families was the experience of struggling
together in pursuit of a common goal,

07:06.222 --> 07:09.793 align:center line:79%
such as taming the wilderness
or earning a living.

07:10.894 --> 07:17.968 align:center line:79%
The family was an organized and conducted
unit of economic production.

07:19.102 --> 07:23.273 align:center line:79%
Today, most families are units
of economic consumption,

07:24.240 --> 07:29.879 align:center line:79%
which does not require a high degree
of family organization and cooperation.

07:31.715 --> 07:34.918 align:center line:81%
As parental influences diminish,

07:35.719 --> 07:41.725 align:center line:79%
Latter-day Saints still have a God-given
responsibility to teach their children

07:41.725 --> 07:45.862 align:center line:79%
to prepare for our family
destiny in eternity.

07:47.230 --> 07:53.636 align:center line:79%
Many of us must do this when not
all of our families are traditional.

07:54.704 --> 08:00.677 align:center line:79%
Divorce, death,
and separation are realities.

08:01.911 --> 08:07.117 align:center line:79%
I experienced that in the family
in which I was raised.

08:08.518 --> 08:11.755 align:center line:81%
My father died when I was seven years old,

08:12.722 --> 08:18.228 align:center line:79%
so my younger brother and sister
and I were raised by a widowed mother.

08:19.496 --> 08:22.198 align:center line:81%
In the most difficult of situations,

08:22.198 --> 08:24.034 align:center line:81%
she pressed on.

08:25.101 --> 08:29.873 align:center line:79%
She was alone and broken,
but with the Lord's help,

08:30.473 --> 08:32.942 align:center line:81%
her powerful teaching of the doctrine

08:32.976 --> 08:39.516 align:center line:79%
of the restored Church guided us.
How she prayed for heavenly assistance

08:39.716 --> 08:44.154 align:center line:79%
in raising her children,
and she was blessed!

08:45.388 --> 08:47.791 align:center line:81%
We were raised in a happy home in

08:47.791 --> 08:52.062 align:center line:79%
which our deceased
father was always a reality.

08:53.063 --> 08:58.234 align:center line:79%
She taught us that we had a father,
and she had a husband,

08:58.735 --> 09:02.972 align:center line:79%
and we would always be a family because
of their temple marriage.

09:04.107 --> 09:06.976 align:center line:81%
Our father was just away temporarily

09:07.577 --> 09:11.147 align:center line:79%
because the Lord had called him
to a different work.

09:13.416 --> 09:16.786 align:center line:79%
I know that many other
families are not so happy.

09:17.620 --> 09:22.826 align:center line:79%
But every single mother can teach
of the love of a Heavenly Father

09:23.393 --> 09:26.796 align:center line:79%
and of the eventual blessings
of a temple marriage.

09:27.564 --> 09:29.265 align:center line:81%
You too can do this.

09:30.633 --> 09:36.306 align:center line:79%
Heavenly Father’s plan assures
this possibility for everyone.

09:38.908 --> 09:41.544 align:center line:81%
We are all grateful for temple marriage

09:41.678 --> 09:47.750 align:center line:79%
and for the prospective blessings
of being sealed as an eternal family.

09:49.119 --> 09:53.256 align:center line:79%
Like my mother, we love
to quote Lehi’s promise to

09:53.323 --> 10:00.396 align:center line:79%
his son Jacob that God “shall consecrate
thine afflictions for thy gain.”

10:01.698 --> 10:04.467 align:center line:79%
That applies to every Latter-
day Saint family,

10:04.467 --> 10:08.171 align:center line:81%
complete or currently incomplete.

10:08.505 --> 10:11.941 align:center line:81%
We are a family church.

10:14.144 --> 10:20.083 align:center line:79%
Our doctrine and our belief in eternal
families strengthen and bond us.

10:21.584 --> 10:26.489 align:center line:79%
I will never forget the promise
of my maternal grandfather Harris,

10:27.290 --> 10:31.628 align:center line:79%
when we children were living
on his farm near Payson, Utah.

10:32.962 --> 10:41.804 align:center line:79%
He gave me the tragic news that my father
had died in faraway Denver, Colorado.

10:43.573 --> 10:45.341 align:center line:81%
I ran into the bedroom

10:46.709 --> 10:50.747 align:center line:79%
and knelt beside the bed,
crying my heart out.

10:52.215 --> 10:57.453 align:center line:79%
Grandpa followed me and went
to his knees beside me and said,

10:57.987 --> 11:00.089 align:center line:81%
“I will be your father.”

11:03.493 --> 11:09.732 align:center line:79%
That tender promise is a powerful example
of what grandparents can do to fill

11:09.732 --> 11:15.338 align:center line:79%
in the gaps when families
lose or are missing a member.

11:20.343 --> 11:23.046 align:center line:81%
Parents, single or married,

11:23.046 --> 11:24.847 align:center line:81%
and others, like grandparents

11:24.847 --> 11:29.419 align:center line:79%
who fill that role for children,
are the master teachers.

11:30.587 --> 11:31.721 align:center line:81%
Their most effective

11:31.788 --> 11:34.424 align:center line:81%
teaching is by example.

11:35.625 --> 11:41.497 align:center line:79%
The family circle is the ideal place
to demonstrate and learn eternal values,

11:41.931 --> 11:47.370 align:center line:79%
such as the importance of marriage
and children, the purpose of life,

11:48.972 --> 11:51.007 align:center line:81%
and the true source of joy.

11:52.775 --> 11:58.348 align:center line:79%
It is also the best place to learn
other essential lessons of life such

11:58.348 --> 12:02.285 align:center line:81%
as kindness, forgiveness, self-control,

12:02.852 --> 12:07.123 align:center line:79%
and the value of education
and honest work.

12:08.992 --> 12:13.162 align:center line:79%
Of course, many Church
members have beloved family members

12:13.696 --> 12:17.934 align:center line:79%
who do not embrace gospel
values and expectations.

12:18.434 --> 12:24.240 align:center line:79%
Such members need our love and patience.
In relating to one another,

12:24.274 --> 12:29.445 align:center line:79%
we should remember that the perfection
we seek is not limited

12:29.712 --> 12:33.516 align:center line:79%
to the stressful
circumstances of mortality.

12:34.517 --> 12:42.525 align:center line:79%
The great teaching in Doctrine and
Covenants section 138, verses 57 to 59,

12:43.192 --> 12:45.395 align:center line:81%
assures us that repentance

12:45.395 --> 12:52.435 align:center line:79%
and spiritual growth can continue in the
Spirit World that follows mortality.

12:53.970 --> 12:58.875 align:center line:79%
More important, as families unite
to strengthen one another,

12:59.409 --> 13:04.647 align:center line:79%
we should all remember that the sins
and inevitable shortcomings

13:04.647 --> 13:09.352 align:center line:79%
all of us experience
in mortality can be forgiven

13:09.686 --> 13:13.523 align:center line:79%
through repentance,
because of the glorious

13:13.523 --> 13:16.526 align:center line:81%
and saving Atonement of Jesus Christ.

13:17.927 --> 13:23.166 align:center line:79%
Our Savior, Jesus Christ, is
our ultimate role model.

13:24.500 --> 13:29.172 align:center line:79%
We will be blessed if we model
our lives after His teachings

13:29.439 --> 13:33.176 align:center line:81%
and self-sacrifice. Following Christ

13:33.176 --> 13:38.448 align:center line:79%
and giving ourselves in service
to one another is the best remedy

13:38.448 --> 13:44.320 align:center line:79%
for the selfishness and individualism
that now seem so common.

13:46.522 --> 13:48.157 align:center line:81%
Parents also have a duty

13:48.157 --> 13:53.363 align:center line:79%
to teach their children practical
knowledge apart from gospel principles.

13:54.163 --> 13:58.034 align:center line:79%
Families unite when they do
meaningful things together.

13:58.768 --> 14:02.205 align:center line:81%
Family gardens build family relationships.

14:02.705 --> 14:06.642 align:center line:79%
Happy family experiences
strengthen family ties.

14:07.276 --> 14:09.912 align:center line:81%
Camping, sports activities,

14:09.912 --> 14:15.885 align:center line:79%
and other recreation are especially
valuable to bond families.

14:16.753 --> 14:22.592 align:center line:79%
Families should organize family
reunions to remember ancestors,

14:23.493 --> 14:25.061 align:center line:81%
which lead to the temple.

14:26.462 --> 14:30.199 align:center line:79%
Parents should educate children
in the basic skills of living,

14:30.733 --> 14:33.202 align:center line:81%
including working in the yard and home.

14:34.270 --> 14:38.875 align:center line:79%
Learning languages is a useful preparation
for missionary service

14:38.875 --> 14:40.676 align:center line:81%
and for modern life.

14:41.844 --> 14:46.516 align:center line:79%
The teachers of these subjects
can be parents or grandparents

14:46.516 --> 14:49.118 align:center line:81%
or members of the extended family.

14:50.753 --> 14:53.623 align:center line:79%
Families flourish when
they learn as a group

14:53.623 --> 14:59.429 align:center line:79%
and counsel together on all matters
of concern to the family and its members.

15:00.997 --> 15:04.967 align:center line:79%
Some may say, “But we have no
time for any of that.”

15:05.835 --> 15:09.205 align:center line:79%
To find time to do
what is truly worthwhile,

15:09.839 --> 15:13.609 align:center line:79%
many parents will find
that they can turn their family

15:13.609 --> 15:18.481 align:center line:79%
on if they all turn
their technologies off.

15:20.950 --> 15:26.622 align:center line:79%
And parents, remember what those children
really want for dinner is time

15:26.622 --> 15:27.623 align:center line:81%
with you.

15:29.625 --> 15:33.429 align:center line:79%
Great blessings come to families
if they pray together,

15:33.429 --> 15:37.366 align:center line:79%
kneeling night and morning
to offer thanks for blessings

15:37.867 --> 15:40.670 align:center line:81%
and to pray over common concerns.

15:41.971 --> 15:47.076 align:center line:79%
Families are also blessed as they worship
together in church services

15:47.343 --> 15:49.679 align:center line:81%
and in other devotional settings.

15:50.613 --> 15:54.684 align:center line:79%
Family bonds are also
strengthened by family stories,

15:55.384 --> 16:01.157 align:center line:79%
creating family traditions,
and sharing sacred experiences.

16:01.791 --> 16:06.028 align:center line:79%
President Spencer W. Kimball
reminded us that “stories

16:06.028 --> 16:11.701 align:center line:79%
of inspiration from our own
lives and those of our forebearers

16:12.101 --> 16:14.804 align:center line:81%
are powerful teaching tools.”

16:16.372 --> 16:22.144 align:center line:79%
They are often the best sources
of inspiration for us and our posterity.

16:24.514 --> 16:29.819 align:center line:79%
I testify of the Lord Jesus Christ,
who is the Only Begotten Son of God,

16:29.852 --> 16:31.320 align:center line:81%
our Eternal Father.

16:32.555 --> 16:36.058 align:center line:79%
He invites us to follow
the covenant path that leads

16:36.058 --> 16:39.395 align:center line:81%
to a heavenly family reunion.

16:40.496 --> 16:44.033 align:center line:79%
The sealing powers of the priesthood
directed by the keys

16:44.033 --> 16:46.068 align:center line:81%
restored in the Kirtland Temple

16:46.435 --> 16:49.872 align:center line:81%
bring families together for eternity.

16:50.773 --> 16:54.944 align:center line:79%
They are currently being exercised
in a growing number of temples

16:54.944 --> 16:57.780 align:center line:81%
of the Lord throughout the world.

16:58.881 --> 17:02.518 align:center line:81%
This is real. Let us be part of it.

17:03.119 --> 17:07.390 align:center line:79%
I pray in the name of Jesus Christ,
amen.

